spi: zynq-qspi: drop unused 'ret' in zynq_qspi_setup_op()

Stable commit fe87fca86911a ("spi: zynq-qspi: Simplify clock handling with
devm_clk_get_enabled()") converts the probe to devm_clk_get_enabled() and
removes the clk_enable() calls from zynq_qspi_setup_op(). Downstream main had
added error handling around those calls (a92908d2a341c, same change as stable
87662cb2e8c5c "spi: zynq-qspi: Add check for clk_enable()"); the conflict was
resolved in favour of the stable removal, since the clocks are now enabled (and
released) by devres and enabling them again here would leak an enable count on
every setup. 'ret' is now unused in zynq_qspi_setup_op().

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-zynq-qspi.c b/drivers/spi/spi-zynq-qspi.c
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-zynq-qspi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-zynq-qspi.c
@@ -435,7 +435,6 @@
 {
 	struct spi_controller *ctlr = spi->controller;
 	struct zynq_qspi *qspi = spi_controller_get_devdata(ctlr);
-	int ret;
 
 	if (ctlr->busy)
 		return -EBUSY;
